{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1177697-pattern-bleeding-question","id":1177697,"title":"Pattern Bleeding question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-20T15:26:42-08:00","id":1177697,"title":"Pattern Bleeding question","content":"What does Pattern Bleeding actually look like? Can you &quot;see&quot; Pattern Bleeding with Spheres other than Prime, and if you can, what does it look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T22:51:36-08:00","id":1177778,"title":"","content":"I presume you probably can't see Pattern Bleeding with Prime at all (unless that's specified somewhere and I missed it).<br /> It's a Life Pattern thing, so it's probably only visible if you can see Life Patterns - i.E. Life 1. Since there is no actually definition of what patterns look like and since it's highly individual to the seeing Mage in question (And really, while many literally see patterns, pattern sensing is not limited to the eyes and might as well be something a Mage simply feels, hears, tastes in the air or even smells..) it is simply something that each character's player needs to come up with in general for their character.<br /> <br /> What I presume though, is that pattern bleeding pretty much manifests at sensing the changed pattern, and how it tears and struggles to return to its original state - ripping itself open as it struggles to do so. Life 1 might make one actually literally see this, it might sound like a discord in the pattern's vibrations, it might 'smell wrong', etc.<br /> <br /> The Prime sphere *might* allow for sensing this as well, now that I think about it, since the aggravated damage from Pattern Bleeding might be the tearing pattern releasing parts of itself as pieces of quintessence into the flow of things. Hmh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T06:13:51-08:00","id":1177827,"title":"","content":"Blood. For the most part you will see blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T06:15:38-08:00","id":1177828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1177697-pattern-bleeding-question?p=1177778#post1177778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Prime sphere *might* allow for sensing this as well, now that I think about it, since the aggravated damage from Pattern Bleeding might be the tearing pattern releasing parts of itself as pieces of quintessence into the flow of things. Hmh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one of the things that can happen when you have Pattern Bleeding it's to spend one point of Quintessence to sustain the changes. Prime can probably detect that &quot;Thaumnivore&quot; status as some sort of quintessential deficiency.<br /> <br /> Anycase, to the layman's eye it may look like a weakening sickness, similar what happens to Bygones, but I don't think there's a propper description of the symptoms, and so the ST should invent something there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T11:53:55-08:00","id":1177907,"title":"","content":"Pattern Bleeding probably &quot;looks&quot; the same as a vast majority of things a mage can &quot;see&quot;: however the mage expects it to.<br /> <br /> The Focus of the mage will dictate how they perceive a Pattern stretched to its breaking point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T15:48:52-08:00","id":1177956,"title":"","content":"Mostly like malnutrition, late stages of tuberculosis, or cancer. The victim will look increasingly thin. Skin loses color and thins, so the victim bruises more easily. Hair falls out or thins. The victim starts getting increasingly tired and lacks motivation and energy. They will complain of increasingly severe pain.<br /> <br /> Prime 1 should reveal that there is a severe problem with the victim's pattern, and that they are leaking or slowing losing primal energy/life force. You should be able to see the energy contrails coming off of them and actively dispersing into the surroundings.<br /> <br /> Life or Entropy 1 should reveal the presence of failing organs and other biological systems. Entropy signs will most commonly appear as dark spots or shadows on the victim, or sometimes as markings or scripts. Life marking will generally show up as discolorations or foul smells.<br /> <br /> As always, there is room for interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T01:10:13-08:00","id":1178382,"title":"","content":"Prime:1 can certainly detect Pattern Bleeding. Remember: Pattern Bleeding can occur for ephemeral as well as physical over-extension of living forms. You can have Pattern Bleeding (Mental Attributes) from enhancing your Per/Int/Wits beyond their normal limits (or human limits, relative to he 5 dot cap) just as with your physical attributes. The underlying metaphysics involved is just that -- <i>underlying.</i> The Pattern in question is &quot;stretching/contorting&quot; in ways that the underlying Prime isn't &quot;moulded&quot; to/for. Life can, of course, detect the overextension of muscle/nerves/et al, and Mind can do the same for mental attributes/faculties; similarly, Spirit could detect a Pattern Bleed resulting from the over-extension of ephemera channeling/empowering a physical form, while Entropy can generally go &quot;ding&quot; when &quot;something's not right/is out of balance&quot;. But Prime can detect when *any* of those things are &quot;not kosher&quot; because of the distortion of the underly Prime involved. (The other Spheres will detect better the *manifestation/type* of bleeding involved -- Life, Mind, etc. -- but Prime can detect something's up with any of them, even if not exactly what/how it's &quot;off&quot; -- though usually Prime:1 and giving the target a casual once-over will usually give one a pretty good idea of what's-what.... lol)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T14:39:08-08:00","id":1185351,"title":"","content":"My character's pattern bleeding is cause by the suppurating, riven remains of their half of a Twin Soul.So I think mind and prime would work, so far as trying to clarify what caused it. I'm not sure how to fix it though. Alleviate it temporarily, fixing it, I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}